# REFERRAL APP — CURSOR RULES
# Read this file, SPEC.md, and PROGRESS.md before every task.

## Project structure
referral/
├── apps/
│   ├── shell/     ← Next.js 15 shell game (Tusok-Tusok Tycoon)
│   └── game-1/    ← future games added here, backend untouched
├── packages/
│   └── api/       ← shared backend: referral engine, payments, fraud, auth
├── docs/          ← scope and PR plan documents
├── SPEC.md        ← full product specification
├── PROGRESS.md    ← current build status (update after every PR)
└── .cursorrules   ← this file

## Non-negotiable rules
- Always read PROGRESS.md at the start of any session before doing anything else
- Always use TypeScript strict mode
- Never hardcode secrets — use environment variables only
- Never put Supabase service role key on the client side (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is server-only)
- Always use the App Router (never pages/)
- All API routes live in apps/shell/app/api/
- Shared backend logic lives in packages/api/src/
- The game (apps/shell) must NEVER import directly from packages/api — use API routes only
- All terminal work, git operations, and PR creation are handled by the agent — zero manual steps
- SQL migrations run via Supabase CLI (supabase db push) — never ask the user to run SQL manually
- After every PR merge, update PROGRESS.md: set Last Completed PR, Next PR, update PR log row to MERGED with date, append to Session Log

## Cursor prompt format
Read .cursorrules first. [This is a code change task only — do not investigate.]
On branch [branch-name], [describe the change]:
1. [Specific change — file, location, what to do]
2. [Specific change]
[Constraints]
Commit and push to [branch-name] and open a PR.
